      "status": "COMPLETED",
      "content": "## Status: Incomplete — `workspace/sc100-filled.pdf` has **not** been created yet\n\n### Completed (verified in this session)\n1. **Source form fully analyzed.** Confirmed `workspace/sc100-blank.pdf` exists; extracted all 103 form fields (`temp/sc100-fields.json`) and the complete 5-page form text (`temp/sc100-text.txt`).\n2. **Complete field map built** (`temp/sc100-fullmap.txt`): qualified names, tooltips, positions, and appearance states for every field.\n3. **Checkbox/radio structure resolved.** The Yes/No and venue checkboxes are standalone fields (each its own field name), grouped only under non-field parent objects.\n4. **pypdf fill mechanics confirmed** by reading the `update_page_form_field_values` source: it matches a field by qualified name **or** short `/T` name; for `/Btn` checkboxes it sets `/AS` to the on-state name (falling back to `/Off`).\n5. **Key pitfall identified.** Multiple checkboxes on page 3 share the short name `Checkbox5cb[0]` (a short-name collision), so they can only be targeted reliably by their full qualified name.\n6. **First fill attempt failed and the cause is understood.** `temp/fill_form.py` reported every field \"missing\" because it matched the full field name against the short annotation `/T`. The fix is known: match by short name per page, and by qualified name for the colliding checkbox group.\n\n### Not completed\n1. **The corrected fill script has not been run successfully**, so **`workspace/sc100-filled.pdf` does not exist yet**.\n2. **Item 3b date mapping was still being confirmed** — which of the three date fields (`Date1[0]`, `Date2[0]`, `Date3[0]`) is \"Date started\" vs. \"Date ended.\" The last script (`temp/page3_raw.py`) was created but not executed.\n\n### Planned field values (from the case description — **not yet written to the PDF**)\n- **Plaintiff:** Joyce He, 655 S Fair Oaks Ave, Sunnyvale, CA 94086, 412-588-6066, he1998@gmail.com\n- **Defendant:** Zhi Chen, 299 W Washington Ave, Sunnyvale, CA 94086, 512-565-8878\n- **Claim amount:** 1500\n- **3a (why owed):** security deposit owed under the signed roommate sublease contract; requested multiple times via text; no response\n- **3b (dates):** 2025-09-30 → 2026-01-19\n- **3c (calculation):** $1,500 = deposit amount stated in the sublease contract\n- **4:** Yes (asked defendant to pay before filing)\n- **5 (venue county):** Santa Clara (defendant lives in Sunnyvale → Santa Clara County)\n- **6 (zip):** 94086\n- **7, 8, 9, 10:** No\n- **Signature:** Joyce He, dated 2026-01-19\n- **Left blank:** court-filled fields (case number, hearing date), optional item 11, and Part 2 (court use)\n\n### Next step (not yet performed)\nRe-run the fill using short-name matching per page (qualified names for the `Checkbox5cb[0]` group), confirm the 3b date-field mapping, write `workspace/sc100-filled.pdf`, then verify the output by re-reading the written field values.",
